              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Honey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Needs some fresh grated black pepper, and we also add a little crushed garlic to the marinade...The onions can be left in the marinade overnight."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ruth Alvis Pierson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used white vinegar and added a bit of dill and sea salt instead. These smelled wonderful cooking and have a great taste to them. I also canned these using the boiling water method to seal the jars for longer storage.",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-23T18:10:44.747Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JUMAHA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Pickled onions never sounded good to me until I had them on a sandwich at a local restaurant. Now I'm hooked! I have been using these to perk up my veggie sandwiches and they are great. I love the new twist. The temp is below zero here in Minnesota and there was no way I was going to get out the grill, so I just simmered the onions in the vinegar solution on the stove until they were soft (about 5-10 min). I cut down the sugar and salt a bit due to personal preference, and added a bit of pickling spice.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-08T12:00:47.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Arentsen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "YUM!! I used a cast iron grill pan brushed with a bit of olive oil to grill the onions the morning of our bbq - so I could let them marinate all day and not have to heat up the grill. Because the onions were warm, and I didn't want to clean another pan - I skipped cooking the vinegar, sugar &amp; salt - and just tossed it all in a mason jar for the day. Absolutely delightful.",
            "datePublished": "2022-05-28T19:00:30.958Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ellie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love these! I did not cook them first. I sliced them in thin vertical pieces and put into glass jar. Cover them with the hot white vinegar mix. They store in the fridge a long time - I keep them in the brine.",
            "datePublished": "2022-03-05T13:47:00.255Z"
          },
